.TH PIXIE 1 "November 2026" "pixie 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pixie \- minimal static HTTP server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pixie
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBpixie\fR starts a static HTTP server using runtime configuration from:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPIXIE_CONFIG\fR (if set)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB./config-pixie.yml\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fB/etc/pixie/config-pixie.yml\fR
.PP
Site directories are read from:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPIXIE_SITES_ROOT\fR (if set; defaults to \fB/etc/pixie/sites\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
the hostname-specific directory, or its \fBdefault\fR subdirectory
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPIXIE_WEB_ROOT\fR overrides hostname selection for a single site.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/pixie/config-pixie.yml
System-wide runtime configuration file.
.TP
.B /etc/pixie/sites
Static sites, stored in \fBdefault/\fR or a directory named for the hostname.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B 2
Configuration initialization error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd (1)
